_:n5823839175df4dd4937b8cab7b1f0bd1b1 <http://id.loc.gov/ontologies/RecordInfo#recordChangeDate> "2016-02-29T00:00:00"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<http://id.loc.gov/authorities/demographicTerms/age> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n            <xhtml:div xmlns:xhtml=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" class=\"aboutCollection\" title=\"About Library of Congress Demographic Group Category: Age [age]:\" property=\"rdfs:comment\">\n                <xhtml:p>The purpose of demographic categories and associated codes is to allow terms that are authorized in Library of Congress Demographic Group Terms (LCDGT) to be collocated at a broad level. The demographic group category codes are three-character lowercase alphabetic strings. They are derived from the first letter of the demographic group category and two additional letters from the word(s) making up the demographic group category name.</xhtml:p>\n                <xhtml:p>Age [age] category is used for the chronological age of the group members (e.g., Adults, Children, Infants).</xhtml:p>\n            </xhtml:div>\n        "^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
<http://id.loc.gov/authorities/demographicTerms/age> <http://www.loc.gov/mads/rdf/v1#isMemberOfMADSScheme> <http://id.loc.gov/authorities/demographicTerms> .
<http://id.loc.gov/authorities/demographicTerms/age> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Age [age]"@en .

